@* ItemList — semantic `<ul>/<li>` rendered via Blazor for
   collections of strings (scope lists, recovery code lists,
   preview sample names, …).

   The markup stays a real <ul> for accessibility and SEO;
   CSS isolation (`.cs-item-list`) replaces the old browser
   default styles so the look matches the rest of the
   Radzen-themed UI. The component exists so consumers
   don't sprinkle plain `<ul>`/`<li>` across the codebase
   — using `<ItemList Items="..." />` makes the pattern
   consistent and lets us tweak the look in one place.

   For lists that need a label per row, the overload that
   takes `RenderFragment` items is the one to use (see the
   items in WorkspaceImport.razor). *@

@code {
    [Parameter] public IEnumerable<string>? Items { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}

@if (Items is not null)
{
    <ul class="cs-item-list">
        @foreach (string item in Items)
        {
            <li>@item</li>
        }
    </ul>
}
else if (ChildContent is not null)
{
    <ul class="cs-item-list">
        @ChildContent
    </ul>
}
